<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="reforging">Reforging for Balance Druid DPS</h3>A new addition in Cataclysm is the ability to reforge. You can change some of one secondary stat to another, for example changing some Hit into Haste if you are over the Hit cap. You can not change to a stat that is already on the item, for example an item with Hit and Haste can not have its Hit changed to Haste, but it can be changed to Mastery or Crit. Keep in mind that you could also change the Haste to Spirit, letting you get both Hit and Spirit on the item.<br/>
<br/>The easiest way to do reforging will be to download the addon Reforgelite Classic and input the stat weights 5.3 on Hit, 3.4 on Haste, 2.4 on Mastery and 2.25 on Crit, with Hit cap of 1742. Leave Spirit at 0 as default settings will automatically detect if you have <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=33596/balance-of-power">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_balanceofpower.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Balance of Power</span></a> and consider Spirit as equal to Hit. Do note that you must be in your Balance spec when using the addon, or you may get wrong results. The addon will calculate how to reforge your gear in a way that gets you as close to 1742 Hit and Spirit as possible while also maximizing how much Haste you end up with. Once it has finished calculating, you can also have the addon do the reforging for you manually. <br/>
<br/>If you want to do it without using addons, your main goals are the same. Try to get Hit as close to 1742 as you can then maximize Haste and then Mastery. In order to do this, you will first want to check how much Hit you have. If it is higher than 1742 you will be looking for items that have Hit or Spirit but not Haste and convert some of your excess to Haste. Make sure you don't overdo it and go below 1742. If you are under 1742 you will want to look for items that have Crit on them and convert them to either Hit or Spirit, avoiding going far abovee 1742. Once your Hit situation have been solved, your next step is to find all items with Crit that has yet to be reforged and reforge them to Haste, or if it already have Haste then reforge to Mastery. Last you want to check every remaining item and if an item have Mastery but not Haste, convert it into Haste.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="dark-intent">Dark Intent</h3>Warlocks can provide the buff <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=85767/dark-intent">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_warlock_focusshadow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dark Intent</span></a>. Having or not having this buff will affect your Haste breakpoints and your gearing, therefore it is recommended to have consistency around wether you are the target of this buff or not. Balance druids are an excellent target due to benefiting a lot from it as well as providing a high uptime to the warlock casting. In T13 the specific thing that changes if you don't have it while in full BiS is that with it you need some haste gems to reach the 3101 Breakpoint.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="haste-breakpoints">Haste Breakpoints</h3>
<b>Note: Regardless of haste breakpoints, haste is always stronger than mastery and crit.</b>
<br/>At certain Haste breakpoints, we get 1 more tick per cast of our dots. These breakpoints will be worth gearing towards if you are close to reaching one. Use of sims have found it to be worth sacrificing as much as 100 Intellect for 100 Haste in order to reach a breakpoint. This is done by changing enchant on Bracers from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=96262/enchant-bracer-mighty-intellect">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulasuperior_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Bracer - Mighty Intellect</span></a> to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=74256/enchant-bracer-greater-speed">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulagood_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Bracer - Greater Speed</span></a> or by changing <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71881/brilliant-queens-garnet">
<img alt="Brilliant Queen's Garnet" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_epicgem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Queen's Garnet</span></a> gems to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71850/reckless-lava-coral">
<img alt="Reckless Lava Coral" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_epicgem_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reckless Lava Coral</span></a> gems. The bis lists are keeping these breakpoints in mind, but when you are working towards them then it can take a lot of manual work to find the needed rating. The table below will display the rating needed for each extra tick.<div class="markup-table-wrapper">
